# Who has to look at a change before it can be merged.
#
# This file only has teeth alongside branch protection - "Require review from Code
# Owners" in Settings > Rules. Without that it is documentation. With it, the paths
# below cannot be changed by whoever pushed them, which is the point: the two things
# most worth a second pair of eyes are the ones that decide what gets deployed and
# what is allowed past the security gate.
#
# Replace @AhmadEbaid001 with the real handles. A team is better than a person for
# everything except the security paths, where a specific name is the point.

*                       @AhmadEbaid001

# The pipeline itself. A change here can turn off every check that protects the
# other paths, so it is reviewed as a security change even when it looks like a
# tidy-up.
/.github/               @AhmadEbaid001
/infra/                 @AhmadEbaid001

# The exception register. Every entry is a decision to ship something a scanner
# objected to; the whole mechanism depends on that being somebody's deliberate,
# reviewed choice rather than a line added to make a red build go green.
/.security/             @AhmadEbaid001
/scripts/security_gate.py  @AhmadEbaid001

# Authentication, sessions and the signed reading chain.
/src/gemp/auth/         @AhmadEbaid001
/src/gemp/ingest/integrity.py  @AhmadEbaid001

# The numbers the paper rests on. A change to the catalog or the parameters changes
# every claim measured against them.
/data/catalog.csv       @AhmadEbaid001
/data/params.yaml       @AhmadEbaid001
